1
00:00:03,377 --> 00:00:05,587
[GUNFIRE ON TV]

2
00:00:05,755 --> 00:00:09,133
If they took all the money they spent
trying to make a decent Hulk movie...

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,927
...they could probably
just make an actual Hulk.

4
00:00:12,678 --> 00:00:14,304
That is apt and amusing.

5
00:00:15,306 --> 00:00:18,392
I think I shall share that
with Amy Farrah Fowler.

6
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:22,104
-She'll appreciate the witticism.
-Thank you.

7
00:00:22,271 --> 00:00:25,482
It will also help improve
her initial impression of you.

8
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:31,155
-So, what's going on with you two?
-Oh, the status is as it always was.

9
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:32,781
She's a girl, she's a friend.

10
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:37,078
She's not my, please forgive me
for doing this, "girlfriend.”

11
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:38,996
Right, right.

12
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:41,665
So you're still just texting
and e-mailing?

13
00:00:41,832 --> 00:00:45,335
You don't feel any need to hang out with
her, you know, be in the same room?

14
00:00:46,462 --> 00:00:48,422
Leonard, you are my best friend.

15
00:00:48,589 --> 00:00:50,257
I've known you for seven years...

16
00:00:50,424 --> 00:00:53,510
...and I can barely tolerate
sitting on the couch with you.

17
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,471
Uh, imagine my attitude...

18
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:59,058
...regarding prolonged physical proximity
to Amy Farrah Fowler.

19
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:01,477
Got it.

20
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:04,772
-Well, I sense judgment on your part.
-No, no.

21
00:01:05,773 --> 00:01:07,524
Maybe a little.

22
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:11,821
May I suggest that your criticism
is based on jealousy?

23
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:14,615
Heh, jealousy? What do I have
to be jealous of?

24
00:01:14,782 --> 00:01:18,535
I have a functioning
and satisfying relationship with a female.

25
00:01:20,496 --> 00:01:22,122
And you have none.

26
00:01:22,832 --> 00:01:24,875
Oh, right. That. Hmm.

27
00:01:25,042 --> 00:01:28,253
Jealousy is an ugly green-eyed monster,
not unlike the Hulk.

28
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:31,382
Who, by the way,
also has a girlfriend.

29
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:33,551
In this iteration, Jennifer Connelly.

30
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:37,346
Whom you may recall as the girlfriend
of Russell Crowe in A Beautiful Mind.

31
00:01:37,513 --> 00:01:40,641
A feel-good romp
if there ever was one.

32
00:01:41,934 --> 00:01:43,018
I'm not jealous.

33
00:01:43,769 --> 00:01:44,811
[GRUNTS]

34
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:46,772
[IMITATES HULK]
Leonard not jealous.

35
00:02:13,674 --> 00:02:15,676
You know, it just occurred to me.

36
00:02:15,843 --> 00:02:18,887
If there are an infinite number
of parallel universes...

37
00:02:19,055 --> 00:02:21,724
...in one of them,
there's probably a Sheldon...

38
00:02:21,891 --> 00:02:25,227
...who doesn't believe
parallel universes exist.

39
00:02:26,103 --> 00:02:28,355
-Probably. What's your point?
-No point.

40
00:02:28,522 --> 00:02:31,483
It's just one of the things
that makes one of the me's chuckle.

41
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:32,693
[CHUCKLES]

42
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:39,070
-What makes you chuckle, Leonard?
-Um, recently? Not much.

43
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:41,618
Is it because of the conflict
that arises. ..

44
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:44,246
...from your desperate need
to pair bond with a woman...

45
00:02:44,413 --> 00:02:47,082
...and the apparent collective decision
of all womankind...

46
00:02:47,249 --> 00:02:49,209
...to deny you that opportunity?

47
00:02:50,753 --> 00:02:52,379
LEONARD:
Um.. ..

48
00:02:52,546 --> 00:02:54,214
Shut up.

49
00:02:54,882 --> 00:02:58,260
SHELDON: You know, when my grandfather
died and Meemaw was alone...

50
00:02:58,427 --> 00:03:01,596
...my Mom arranged for her
to visit a center three times a week. ..

51
00:03:01,764 --> 00:03:05,142
...where she could socialize
with other lonely people.

52
00:03:05,309 --> 00:03:06,435
It's very nice.

53
00:03:06,602 --> 00:03:09,980
They discuss current events,
play bridge, get a hot meal.

54
00:03:10,147 --> 00:03:14,234
LEONARD: That sounds lovely.
SHELDON: Um, it is if you like bridge.

55
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:17,029
Do you like bridge, Leonard?

56
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:19,907
LEONARD: Sheldon, I'm just
not dating someone right now.

57
00:03:20,074 --> 00:03:23,035
I don't need to go
to a seniors' center.

58
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:27,748
Meemaw resisted at first,
but now she loves it.

59
00:03:27,915 --> 00:03:31,168
Fine. If I don't meet someone soon,
you can put me in a home.

60
00:03:31,335 --> 00:03:35,255
It's not a home.
It's a senior center.

61
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:38,134
We'd never put Meemaw
in a home.

62
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:41,595
-Hey, guys.
-Hey.

63
00:03:41,762 --> 00:03:44,973
All right, I'll bow to social pressure.
Hey.

64
00:03:46,225 --> 00:03:47,267
[CELL PHONE RINGS]

65
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:49,311
Excuse me.
That's my girlfriend Bernadette.

66
00:03:49,478 --> 00:03:52,689
I assigned her own ring tone.
"Bernadette" by The Four Tops.

67
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:54,942
Hello, Bernadette.

68
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:58,821
When I call him,
his phone plays "Brown Eyed Girl"...

69
00:04:00,614 --> 00:04:02,991
...which now
that I think about it is not so good.

70
00:04:03,617 --> 00:04:05,577
You realize
he's just rubbing our noses...

71
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,663
...In the fact that he has a girlfriend
and we don't.

72
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,289
You mean you don't.

73
00:04:10,624 --> 00:04:12,250
You have a girlfriend?
How could you?

74
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:16,505
-You can't even speak to women.
-Uh, two words: Deaf chick.

75
00:04:17,673 --> 00:04:20,967
It doesn't matter if I can't talk
because she can't hear me.

76
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:24,179
-What?
-That's what she said.

77
00:04:26,182 --> 00:04:28,601
Great. You have a girlfriend,
Howard has a girlfriend...

78
00:04:28,768 --> 00:04:29,894
-...Sheldon's got a--
SHELDON: Ahem.

79
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:32,520
-Girl who's a friend.
-Thank you.

80
00:04:33,230 --> 00:04:35,649
What about you, Stuart?
You have a girlfriend yet?

81
00:04:35,816 --> 00:04:38,527
Oh, yeah.
Yeah, I met her at Comic-Con.

82
00:04:38,694 --> 00:04:41,697
The one place in the world where saying
"I own a comic book store". ..

83
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:43,323
...Is an actual pick-up line.

84
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:47,244
-Oh. Well, good for you.
-Not really. She's horrible.

85
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:51,832
When she wants to have sex, she puts on
her plus-size Wonder Woman costume...

86
00:04:51,999 --> 00:04:55,877
...and shouts, "Who wants to take a ride
in my invisible plane?"

87
00:04:57,546 --> 00:05:01,091
-Why don't you just break up with her?
-Heh, no, I can't.

88
00:05:01,258 --> 00:05:04,678
-Why not?
-Because then I'd be alone. Like you.

89
00:05:06,847 --> 00:05:10,267
Dude, why don't you just invoke
your girlfriend pact with Wolowitz?

90
00:05:10,434 --> 00:05:14,729
Uh, because I don't need his girlfriend
to set me up with one of her girlfriends.

91
00:05:14,897 --> 00:05:18,233
I'm perfectly capable
of finding a girl on my own.

92
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:21,736
Oh, Leonard. You remind me
of the funny old story about a man...

93
00:05:21,904 --> 00:05:24,406
...who walks into
3 women's correctional institution. ..

94
00:05:24,573 --> 00:05:26,074
...with a stack of paperwork...

95
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:28,911
...that would allow
the female convicts to go free.

96
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:33,415
You're saying I couldn't get laid in a
women's prison with a handful of pardons.

97
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:36,209
Are you gonna
let me tell the story or not?

98
00:05:40,422 --> 00:05:44,259
-Leonard? Are you sleeping?
-No.

99
00:05:44,426 --> 00:05:46,177
-Are you ill?
-No.

100
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:49,889
Are you depressed because you're
alone and no one loves you?

101
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:52,476
I don't know. Maybe.

102
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:56,063
I want you to know that I'm genuinely
concerned about your well-being.

103
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:57,940
-Thank you.
You're welcome.

104
00:05:58,107 --> 00:06:01,110
But it's still no reason
to have your feet in my spot.

105
00:06:04,446 --> 00:06:06,281
AMY [OVER LAPTOP]:
May I offer an observation?

106
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:10,035
What the hell?
How long has she been there?

107
00:06:10,202 --> 00:06:12,245
Since we got home
from the comic book store.

108
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:13,872
That was two hours ago.

109
00:06:14,039 --> 00:06:16,583
As per your suggestion,
we're hanging out.

110
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:19,461
Quite frankly, I don't see
what all the hoopla is about.

111
00:06:19,628 --> 00:06:20,712
Go on, Amy.

112
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,464
From a neurobiological standpoint...

113
00:06:22,631 --> 00:06:25,175
...you may be alone
because your psychological state...

114
00:06:25,342 --> 00:06:28,803
...Is causing an actual pheromone-based
stink of desperation.

115
00:06:30,222 --> 00:06:32,015
-Did you know that, Leonard?
-No.

116
00:06:32,224 --> 00:06:33,808
I did.

117
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:36,603
I understand that
some people find mates...

118
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:39,105
...In social gathering places
such as bars or taverns.

119
00:06:39,273 --> 00:06:40,774
Have you tried a bar or tavern?

120
00:06:40,941 --> 00:06:43,026
No, I'm not gonna
pick up a woman in a bar.

121
00:06:43,235 --> 00:06:45,278
Wise decision. You see, Amy...

122
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:48,782
...success at a bar
is based on classic male attributes..

123
00:06:48,949 --> 00:06:51,868
...such as:
height, strength, attractiveness...

124
00:06:52,036 --> 00:06:55,998
...the ability to hold one's liquor
and throw darts, separately or together.

125
00:06:56,165 --> 00:06:59,543
Leonard has none of these attributes,
right, Leonard?

126
00:07:01,545 --> 00:07:03,255
Right.

127
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:06,883
That's not true of all bars.
Juice bars for example.

128
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:08,969
Oh, good point, Amy.

129
00:07:09,136 --> 00:07:10,762
Yeah. Building on your premise...

130
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:14,058
...Leonard could frequent sushi bars,
salad bars...

131
00:07:14,266 --> 00:07:16,476
...oyster bars,
the Apple Genius Bar.

132
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:19,063
-What are you doing?
-Keep going, I'm listening.

133
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:22,357
That was rude.

134
00:07:22,858 --> 00:07:24,150
He does it all the time.

135
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:27,988
He's a cornucopia
of social awkwardness.

136
00:07:28,405 --> 00:07:30,698
Cornucopia, what a mellifluous word.

137
00:07:30,866 --> 00:07:33,535
-Let's make that our word of the day.
-Agreed.

138
00:07:33,702 --> 00:07:35,578
And we'll use mellifluous tomorrow.

139
00:07:36,413 --> 00:07:38,832
Well, I have to void my bladder.

140
00:07:38,999 --> 00:07:40,917
It was nice
spending this time with you.

141
00:07:41,085 --> 00:07:44,546
AMY: Wait. I have a request.
-Yes?

142
00:07:44,713 --> 00:07:48,925
-I'd like you to meet my mother.
-I see. Can I get back to you on that?

143
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:52,513
-Certainly. Good night.
-Good night.

144
00:07:57,559 --> 00:08:02,059
SHELDON:
Leonard. Leonard--

145
00:08:02,398 --> 00:08:06,693
Leonard. Leonard--

146
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:09,404
-Leonard. Leonard.
Yeah. What?

147
00:08:09,571 --> 00:08:12,323
Amy Farrah Fowler
has asked me to meet her mother.

148
00:08:12,491 --> 00:08:16,203
-Yeah? So?
“What does that mean?

149
00:08:16,745 --> 00:08:19,414
You know how you're always saying
that Amy is a girl...

150
00:08:19,581 --> 00:08:22,417
-...who is a friend and not your girlfriend??
-Uh-huh.

151
00:08:22,584 --> 00:08:24,335
You can't say that anymore.

152
00:08:27,339 --> 00:08:28,423
SHELDON:
What?

153
00:08:28,590 --> 00:08:31,426
LEONARD: She obviously wants to
take your relationship to the next level.

154
00:08:31,593 --> 00:08:35,597
SHELDON: Ugh, I don't want the next level.
I like this level.

155
00:08:36,098 --> 00:08:38,266
Fix it for me.

156
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:40,811
Me? How am I supposed to fix it?

157
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:44,272
Simple. You want a girlfriend.
Amy wants to be someone's girlfriend.

158
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:47,359
Take her off my hands.
I give you my blessing.

159
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,444
That is insane.

160
00:08:49,611 --> 00:08:52,488
You're right. It would never work.
Amy finds you tedious.

161
00:08:53,115 --> 00:08:55,117
-Okay, good luck.
“W-- Wait.

162
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:56,576
What am I supposed to do?

163
00:08:56,744 --> 00:08:59,371
Have you considered telling her
how you feel?

164
00:08:59,538 --> 00:09:02,624
Leonard, I'm a physicist,
not a hippie.

165
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:08,589
All right, well, let me see if I can
explain your situation using physics.

166
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:11,759
What would you be
if you were attached to another object...

167
00:09:11,925 --> 00:09:15,970
...by an inclined plane
wrapped helically around an axis?

168
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:18,515
Screwed.

169
00:09:20,642 --> 00:09:22,769
There you go.

170
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:28,942
Amy's right, he is tedious.

171
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:36,992
MRS. WOLOWITZ:
Howard, get the door!

172
00:09:38,285 --> 00:09:39,828
HOWARD:
Why can't you get it?

173
00:09:39,995 --> 00:09:44,495
MRS. WOLOWITZ: You know I'm doing
a bowel cleanse for my colonoscopy.

174
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:50,835
I'm like an upside-down volcano here.

175
00:09:53,008 --> 00:09:55,552
Oh, hey, heh, I hope you didn't hear that.

176
00:09:55,719 --> 00:09:57,637
The volcano thing? No.

177
00:09:58,764 --> 00:10:01,600
What's with the T-shirt?
You're working at the Apple store now?

178
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:03,852
Well, uh, no, it's just something
I threw on.

179
00:10:04,019 --> 00:10:06,855
I know all your shirts,
that's not one of.. ..

180
00:10:07,022 --> 00:10:10,650
You were pretending to work at the Genius
Bar to pick up women, weren't you?

181
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:13,654
Yeah.

182
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:18,450
Turns out they guard the iPods,
but they don't guard the shirts.

183
00:10:18,617 --> 00:10:21,620
-So how'd it go?
-It was going well.

184
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:24,623
I was showing this super hot girl
how to boot up in safe mode...

185
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,750
...the manager got suspicious and....

186
00:10:26,917 --> 00:10:31,417
Well, long story short,
they really do have a little jail in the mall.

187
00:10:32,339 --> 00:10:35,258
Just FYI, don't try to go back
with a fake mustache.

188
00:10:35,467 --> 00:10:39,554
I mean, they may not really be geniuses,
but they see right through that.

189
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:42,641
I wanna invoke the girlfriend pact,
Howard.

190
00:10:42,808 --> 00:10:43,850
You that desperate?

191
00:10:44,017 --> 00:10:46,227
No, uh, I just....
You know, I want what you have.

192
00:10:46,395 --> 00:10:48,063
You know,
I want a woman in my life.

193
00:10:48,230 --> 00:10:52,730
MRS. WOLOWITZ: Holy Moses,
how much liquid can be in one tuchus?

194
00:10:57,072 --> 00:10:59,407
To be clear, I meant Bernadette,
not your mother.

195
00:10:59,575 --> 00:11:01,660
No, I know what you meant.

196
00:11:05,247 --> 00:11:08,208
Well, I'm off to meet
Bernadette's friend. How do I look?

197
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:10,836
As if one of the plants...

198
00:11:11,003 --> 00:11:14,256
...from Invasion of the Body Snatchers
duplicated you in every way...

199
00:11:14,423 --> 00:11:16,758
...only with an absurd amount
of hair gel.

200
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:19,427
What are you working on?

201
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:22,556
I'm removing my digital footprint
from the Internet...

202
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:26,184
...50 Amy Farrah Fowler can't find me
and compel me to meet her mother.

203
00:11:26,351 --> 00:11:29,437
-Oh. You're going off the grid.
-Exactly.

204
00:11:29,605 --> 00:11:32,524
The old Unabomber approach. Kudos.

205
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:37,446
Thank you. I've also sent
Amy a relationship termination notice...

206
00:11:37,613 --> 00:11:41,366
...and changed my cell phone
number and e-mail address.

207
00:11:41,533 --> 00:11:43,117
What if she just comes over?

208
00:11:43,285 --> 00:11:46,788
She'll get lost.
We no longer live at 2311 Los Robles.

209
00:11:46,955 --> 00:11:51,042
We now live at 311 Los Robles.

210
00:11:54,671 --> 00:11:57,674
You changed the address
on the building? What about mail?

211
00:11:57,841 --> 00:12:00,760
No worries, I explained
my predicament to our letter carrier.

212
00:12:00,928 --> 00:12:04,306
He was sympathetic. His exact words
were, "Got your back, Jack.

213
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:06,725
Bitches be crazy.”

214
00:12:08,018 --> 00:12:09,561
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

215
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:15,692
LEONARD: Who is it?
AMY: Amy Farrah Fowler.

216
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:22,699
-Darn! She found me.
-She's been here before.

217
00:12:24,576 --> 00:12:27,161
The only flaw
in an otherwise perfect plan.

218
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:31,541
-Now get my back, Jack.
-What do you wanna do?

219
00:12:31,708 --> 00:12:33,334
-Tell her I'm not here.
-Where are you?

220
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:35,670
I don't know.
You'll have to devise a scenario...

221
00:12:35,837 --> 00:12:37,588
...that plausibly explains my absence...

222
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:42,051
...keeping in mind that the key
to a good lie lies in the details.

223
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:43,803
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

224
00:12:55,023 --> 00:12:58,818
-Hi, Amy. Sheldon's not here.
-All right.

225
00:13:04,241 --> 00:13:05,992
Way to go on the details.

226
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:12,540
-Thanks again for doing this, Bernadette.
-Oh, I take pacts very seriously.

227
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:13,792
One time at my lab...

228
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:17,045
...a Petri dish of genetically modified
super-virus went missing.

229
00:13:17,212 --> 00:13:18,838
That day, we made a pinky swear...

230
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:22,551
...never to admit that we crossed
Ebola with the common cold.

231
00:13:23,468 --> 00:13:27,388
